```
layout(local_size_x = 256) in;
layout(std430, binding = 0) readonly buffer VecA { float a[]; };
layout(std430, binding = 1) readonly buffer VecB { float b[]; };
layout(std430, binding = 2) writeonly buffer Res { float result[]; };
```
`main()` multiplies `a[gid] * b[gid]`, stores it in shared memory, performs a binary reduction with `barrier()` between steps, and finally `atomicAdd(result[0], cache[0])` once per work group. All ids use `uint`, no deprecated qualifiers, and the shader compiles successfully on any OpenGL 4.3 driver.

