Why the list is not updated
---------------------------
1. Your +page.svelte gets its `notes` array from the `load()` function in +page.server.js.
2. When you submit the *delete* form with `use:enhance`, SvelteKit upgrades the POST to a `fetch`, so **the browser never navigates away**.
3. Because there is no navigation, SvelteKit **does NOT re-run `load()`**. The JSON you return from the action is stored in the **`form` store**, *not* in `data`, so the component keeps rendering the stale `data.notes` it already has.

How to refresh the UI — pick one of these
-----------------------------------------
A. Invalidate the page after the action (most common)
```svelte
<!-- +page.svelte -->
<script>
  import { enhance } from "$app/forms";
  import { invalidateAll } from "$app/navigation";

  // Re-run every load function on this page once the delete succeeds
  const enhanceDelete = enhance({
    after() {
      invalidateAll();
    }
  });
</script>

{#each data.notes as note (note.id)}
  <form action="?/delete" method="post" use:enhance={enhanceDelete}>
    <input type="hidden" name="id" value={note.id} />
    <button aria-label="delete {note.title}">🗑️</button>
  </form>
{/each}
```
```js
// +page.server.js
export const actions = {
  delete: async ({ request, locals }) => {
    const { id } = Object.fromEntries(await request.formData());
    await locals.db.note.delete({ where: { id } });
    return { success: true }; // goes into the form store
  }
};

export const load = async ({ locals }) => {
  return {
    notes: await locals.db.note.findMany({ orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" } })
  };
};
```

B. Return the updated list from the action
```js
// +page.server.js (inside delete action)
return {
  updated: await locals.db.note.findMany()
};
```
```svelte
<script>
  import { form } from "$app/forms";
  export let data;
  $: notes = $form?.updated ?? data.notes;
</script>
```

C. Quick-and-dirty: remove `use:enhance`
If you drop the directive, the browser makes a normal POST; the page fully reloads and `load()` runs again.

Pitfalls to avoid
-----------------
• Forgetting `import { invalidateAll } from "$app/navigation";`
• Calling `invalidate()` with the wrong argument.
• Returning new data but still reading `data.notes` instead of the `form` store.

Key takeaway: `use:enhance` skips a navigation, so re-run `load()` with `invalidate*()` or feed fresh data through the `form` store to keep your notes list in sync.

