Explanation
-----------
The iterator stores previously discovered primes (Vec<u64>) so each new candidate only needs to be trial-divided by primes ≤ √candidate. After 2 we skip even numbers, halving the work. The algorithm is O(n log n) time and O(π(n)) memory, adequate for on-demand generation while avoiding the unbounded memory usage of a full sieve. The code uses safe Rust, compiles on stable 1.70+, contains unit tests, and can be extended to u128 by replacing the type aliases.
